**Protocol & Parsing**
Every fix from errors 9–15, 17–18, 22, 40–43, 60–62, 71, 81–83, 89–91, 106–110, 123, 127–128 is addressed: HTTP version is now validated (`HTTP/1.0` / `HTTP/1.1` only), method token is validated against the RFC set, extra tokens after the version cause rejection, `Host` header is required for HTTP/1.1, duplicate `Content-Length` with differing values is rejected, `Transfer-Encoding` is rejected with `400`, leading-zeros/non-digit characters in `Content-Length` value are rejected, NUL and non-`/` first-character paths are rejected, integer overflow on `header_end + 4 + content_length` is guarded with `std.math.add` .

**Buffer & Memory**
Errors 6, 38, 75–77 fixed: initial allocation is `8192` bytes and doubled geometrically on growth, eliminating the \(O(n^2)\) realloc-from-zero pattern. All three build helpers (`buildBytezPayload`, `buildErrorJson`, `proxyChatRequest`) now use `std.ArrayList` with `toOwnedSlice()` — a single allocation, zero double-copy.

